#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186216937 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c0a1cb-fb61-52f6-a966-f47b0984daa0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7ad71ab7-0054-5b72-b82b-5a1010be8e09" :question/math-academy-id "e-21079" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n1. $y' = 4xy^2 - 3y + 1$\n2. $y' - 2y = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x)$\n3. $y' = e^xy^3 + y - x$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Riccati differential equation with\n$a(x) = 4x, \\qquad b(x)=-3, \\qquad c(x)=1$.\n- Equation II is a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n$y' = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x) + 2y$.\nThis is a Riccati differential equation with\n$a(x) = x^2 + 5, \\qquad b(x)=2, \\qquad c(x)=\\sin(x)$.\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n$y' = e^xy^3 + y - x$.\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a $y^3$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186216938 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c5fc503-d0bb-54e3-8192-dbb30aef1d27" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Riccati Differential Equation to a Bernoulli Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "97fae947-db0f-55bd-9b9c-4095ff0f64a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21080" :question/problem "The function $y_0(x) = 1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n$y' = 3y^2 - 7y + 4$.\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n$\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$, and the value of $n$." :question/worked-solution "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x)\n$$\n\nIn our case, $y_0(x) = 1$. Since $y_0'(x) = 0$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 1 \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z'\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' = 3(z + 1)^2 - 7(z + 1) + 4\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^{′} &= 3(z + 1)^{2} - 7(z + 1) + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} &= 3z^{2} - z \\\\\nz^{′} + z &= 3z^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d} z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x) = 1, \\qquad Q(x) = 3, \\qquad n = 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186216939 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb23c291-a2fb-5e57-bbc9-7b2c02d0a1ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "d9bbb25d-0622-5b36-bcfa-a8375e326576" :question/math-academy-id "e-21081" :question/problem "Given that $y_0(x) = 4x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$y' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." :question/worked-solution "The equation\n\n$$\ny' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x) = 2x, \\qquad b(x) = -16x^2, \\qquad c(x) = 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x)\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\ny_0(x) = 4x\n$$\n\nSince $y_0'(x) = 4$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 4x \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z' + 4\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' + 4 = 2x\\,(z + 4x)^2 - 16x^2 (z + 4x) + 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^{′} + 4 &= 2x(z^{2} + 8xz + 16x^{2}) - 16x^{2}(z + 4x) + 32x^{3} + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} + 4 &= 2xz^{2} + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} &= 2xz^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 2xz^{2} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{z^{2}}\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 2x \\\\\n∫\\frac{1}{z^{2}}\\frac{dz}{dx}dx &= ∫2xdx \\\\\n∫z^{-2}dz &= ∫2xdx \\\\\n- \\frac{1}{z} &= x^{2} + C \\\\\nz &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z = y-4x$ to recover the initial variable $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} \\\\\ny - 4x &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} + 4x \\\\\n&= 4x - \\frac{1}{x^{2} + C}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c0a1cb-fb61-52f6-a966-f47b0984daa0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a1fe1d-221d-5c05-b40d-2f05b90e24da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216523} {:answer/id #uuid "e0057490-e9e6-55b0-8fe0-f699acd84c07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216524} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fa6476-305f-5498-ae1a-219897b54fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216525} {:answer/id #uuid "3b59a381-b1f6-570d-bd0f-7121172b7090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216526} {:answer/id #uuid "54450020-0e39-561a-804a-79f86a32e3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2fa6476-305f-5498-ae1a-219897b54fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216525} :answer-field/id #uuid "424cc51c-827f-58e3-b26a-23d89ae1df45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216522}] :question/id #uuid "41edd4a5-308f-5a31-bafd-5300fefbb7ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-333306" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n1. $y^{′} = y^{3} - 2xy + 4$\n2. $y^{′} = 6xy^{2} + 3y - x$\n3. $y^{′} + 5y = 2x^{2}y^{2} + 7$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c5fc503-d0bb-54e3-8192-dbb30aef1d27" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Riccati Differential Equation to a Bernoulli Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ae04aa79-961a-575a-9cd6-8279e3980e86" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216528} {:answer-field/id #uuid "f6079969-02a4-5291-838f-5c62fa2b1cbb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216529} {:answer-field/id #uuid "25520bf5-ddf9-5014-8522-6b3884046d75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216530}] :question/id #uuid "97143866-a7bb-5489-993f-170b6d862f7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-333607" :question/problem "The function $y_{0}(x) = 1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n$y^{′} = y^{2} - 3y + 2$.\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n$\\frac{dz}{dx} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^{n}$\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$, and the value of $n$.$P(x) =$\n{{field-1}}\n$, Q(x) =$\n{{field-2}}\n$, n =$\n{{field-3}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb23c291-a2fb-5e57-bbc9-7b2c02d0a1ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Riccati Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e876a44-04d8-586e-8a6e-9276b967fef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216532} {:answer/id #uuid "047c2ef1-729e-5440-9d73-7bc16cbad0d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{1}{2x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216533} {:answer/id #uuid "166ea331-4854-530e-ae02-450a52b0c437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216534} {:answer/id #uuid "405ecbae-819f-5a22-a93b-37b7072a1182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{2}{x - C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216535} {:answer/id #uuid "6b400c9a-f042-57e1-80cb-5b27f353ca0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{2}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "166ea331-4854-530e-ae02-450a52b0c437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{1}{x + C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216534} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9bd62a2-882f-5ad3-b3e6-3af72b1a9d02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216531}] :question/id #uuid "c9b2868a-b882-5b68-b22b-3bc42a1c4dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-333805" :question/problem "Given that $y_{0}(x) = \\frac{2}{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$y^{′} = y^{2} - \\frac{4}{x}y + \\frac{2}{x^{2}}$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation."}]}
